 to the constraint $g(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}=48.$ \n\nSince $f(x,y,z)$ is continuous and the constraint is closed and bounded, $f(x,y,z)$ reaches a global maximum and a global minimum on the constraint. \n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z),\\,g(x,y,z)=48\n$$\n\nWe start by solving the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x}(x,y,z),{f}_{y}(x,y,z),{f}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x}(x,y,z),{g}_{y}(x,y,z),{g}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ \\\\ ⟨0,3,3⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨2x,4y,8z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we cannot have $\\lambda =0$ since this leads to a contradiction in the above equation. Therefore, assuming $\\lambda \\ne 0,$ we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0=2\\lambda x \\\\ 3=4\\lambda y \\\\ 3=8\\lambda z\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ y=\\frac{3}{4\\lambda } \\\\ z=\\frac{3}{8\\lambda }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute our expressions for $x,\\,y$ and $z$ into the condition $g(x,y,z)=48$ and solve for $\\lambda ,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =48 \\\\ {0}^{2}+2(\\frac{9}{16{\\lambda }^{2}})+4(\\frac{9}{64{\\lambda }^{2}}) & =48 \\\\ \\frac{9}{8{\\lambda }^{2}}+\\frac{9}{16{\\lambda }^{2}} & =48 \\\\ \\frac{18}{16{\\lambda }^{2}}+\\frac{9}{16{\\lambda }^{2}} & =48 \\\\ \\frac{27}{16{\\lambda }^{2}} & =48 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =\\frac{9}{256} \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find $y$ and $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny=\\pm 4,\\,z=\\pm 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(0,-4,-2),\\,(0,4,2).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at each of these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $\\,(x,y,z)\\,$ | $\\,(0,-4,-2)\\,$ | $\\,(0,4,2)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,f(x,y,z)\\,$ | $\\,-18\\,$ | $\\,18\\,$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a maximum value at $(0,4,2),$ and its maximum value is $18.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1045 "Lagrange Multipliers With One Constraint" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186483465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482810 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "da0cbfc1-126a-53bb-9e82-05a1649265b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482822 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482822 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482822 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "077e60b6-8dfd-5425-af73-cfd611ef7918" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482839 #edb/ref 1080 "-9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482839 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482839 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "112e5b58-a689-5138-b33f-e47c56e7167c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482914 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482914 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482914 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3c313004-6208-55c4-a29e-409a760d3bd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482920 #edb/ref 1080 "11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482920 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482920 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "40fc280e-d5f1-5a84-9cfc-9c3ad50813fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482952 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482952 #edb/ref 1082 #e